</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>On-Orbit Experiments (ISS)</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">ASTREA was subsequently deployed aboard the International Space Station (ISS) to validate feasibility in a true operational environment (See <a href="#S3.SS5.SSS2" title="3.5.2 On-Orbit Deployment (ISS) ‣ 3.5 Experimental Environments: Ground Lab and ISS Deployment ‣ 3 Experimental Design and Implementation ‣ ASTREA: Introducing Agentic Intelligence for Orbital Thermal Autonomy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5.2</span></a>). In this experiment, the agentic system exhibited shorter episode durations than the RL-only baseline, but also achieved a reduction in the number of thermal violations. CPU usage showed a slight increase when the LLM-agent was active (Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.2 On-Orbit Experiments (ISS) ‣ 4 Results &amp; Analysis ‣ ASTREA: Introducing Agentic Intelligence for Orbital Thermal Autonomy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S4.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Representative results from on-orbit experiments aboard the ISS.</span></figcaption>
